{"name":"Light Chiffon","hex":"#f4e7e5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"chiffon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A lightweight, balanced plain-woven sheer fabric, or gauze, like gossamer, woven of alternate S- and Z-twist crepe (high-twist) yarns made of silk, polyester, or cotton.","Any purely ornamental accessory on a woman's dress, such as a bunch of ribbon, lace, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chiffon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chiffon (fabric)","blocks":[{"text":"Chiffon, from the French word chiffe which means \"cloth or rag\"; is a lightweight, balanced plain-woven sheer fabric, or gauze, like gossamer, woven of alternate S- and Z-twist crepe (high-twist) yarns. Crepe yarn tends to have a tighter twist than standard yarns. The twist in the crepe yarns puckers the fabric slightly in both directions after weaving, giving it some stretch and a slightly rough feel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Lillian_Gish_2.jpg/330px-Lillian_Gish_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chiffon_(fabric)","wikidata":"Q691189"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light","wikidata":"Q9128"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/No8633No8638No8626No9651.png/500px-No8633No8638No8626No9651.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/No8633No8638No8626No9651.png/1280px-No8633No8638No8626No9651.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/No8633No8638No8626No9651.png/500px-No8633No8638No8626No9651.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Coat and skirt street suit of gray chiffon broadcloth with embroidery and lace decoration (1905)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANo8633No8638No8626No9651.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/1970s_Givenchy_cocktail_dress%2C_orange_printed_silk_chiffon_03.jpg/120px-1970s_Givenchy_cocktail_dress%2C_orange_printed_silk_chiffon_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/1970s_Givenchy_cocktail_dress%2C_orange_printed_silk_chiffon_03.jpg/250px-1970s_Givenchy_cocktail_dress%2C_orange_printed_silk_chiffon_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/1970s_Givenchy_cocktail_dress%2C_orange_printed_silk_chiffon_03.jpg/120px-1970s_Givenchy_cocktail_dress%2C_orange_printed_silk_chiffon_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnai